&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Bitwarden is the trusted identity security leader for millions of users worldwide, empowering enterprises, developers, and individuals to securely manage and share sensitive information anywhere. Bitwarden makes it easy for all users to extend robust security across their devices with password management, secrets management, and passwordless and passkey innovations. The company is headquartered in Santa Barbara, California. Learn more at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://bitwarden.com&quot;&gt;bitwarden.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;As we scale our India Engineering Centre of Excellance we are looking for a Senior Software Development Engineer in Test (SDET) to gate Bitwarden Products and driving a total-quality approach to software development and delivery. You will contribute directly to the future of the Bitwarden products, while working with a great team and an amazing open-source community. This role is primarily for someone strong in C#, test automation framework design, CI/CD integration, and engineering-quality test code.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain automated test scripts for web, browser extension, mobile, desktop and CLI applications using C# with Selenium/Appium.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement robust, scalable, reusable, and maintainable test automation frameworks across multiple application types.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate automated tests into the CI/CD pipeline and ensure their reliable execution in build and delivery workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with development and QA teams to understand requirements, identify test scenarios, and automate for comprehensive coverage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute automated tests, analyze results, and surface defects, performance issues, and areas for improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review test automation code to uphold coding standards, best practices, and maintainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish guidelines and processes for testing community and internal product contributions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in Agile/Scrum ceremonies, reporting automation progress, blockers, and upcoming sprint plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide mentorship and guidance to junior team members on automation best practices and frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document frameworks and processes to support knowledge sharing and long-term maintainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong C# proficiency with substantial production test-automation experience (4 - 7 years).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Senior automation architecture capability: scalable, reusable, maintainable frameworks; readable/testable code; debugging and edge-case handling across multiple application types.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CI/CD integration ownership: embedding automated tests into build/delivery pipelines and keeping them stable and trustworthy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid command of software testing principles and methodologies, with clear collaboration in a distributed, cross-functional team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mobile test automation with Appium.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remote/cloud device and browser testing (Sauce Labs, BrowserStack, or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SaaS, security, identity, privacy, or developer-facing product experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience testing alongside and integrating with backend/API services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentoring junior automation engineers and reviewing test code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in global, distributed technical teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on AI/ML experience beyond tooling (evaluating or applying AI-generated tests).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an opportunity to play a foundational role in shaping our India Engineering COE from the ground up.&amp;nbsp;Our user community loves us and we love them. Come to work each day with a sense of purpose as we bring a more secure internet experience to everyone from our friends and family to the world’s largest organizations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Become an expert. You’ll get immersed in the prominent technology markets of security and open source software. You&#39;ll work alongside talented global teams, solve meaningful engineering challenges, influence how we scale our engineering organization &amp;amp; contribute to products used by customers around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;re passionate about building exceptional teams, enabling engineering excellence, and making a lasting impact within a fast-growing engineering company, we&#39;d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Employer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are committed to fostering an inclusive workplace where everyone can do their best work. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds and make employment decisions based on skills, experience, qualifications, and business needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Bitwarden empowers enterprises, developers, and individuals to securely store and share&amp;nbsp;sensitive data. With a transparent, open-source approach to password management, secrets&amp;nbsp;management, and passwordless and passkey innovations, Bitwarden makes it easy for users to&amp;nbsp;extend robust security practices across all online activities. Founded in 2016 with headquarters&amp;nbsp;in Santa Barbara, California, Bitwarden is supported by a passionate global community of&amp;nbsp;security experts and enthusiasts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Site Reliability Engineer - FedRAMP at Bitwarden, you will be responsible for operating and building Bitwarden Gov. You will be responsible for every element of the infrastructure and operations within the new region, including availability, performance, change management, monitoring, incident response, and capacity planning, all while maintaining a strong emphasis on security/compliance/governance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for team members who can own the current and future state of our Gov cloud&amp;nbsp;infrastructure distributed across multiple cloud providers, design and build out new&amp;nbsp;infrastructure, as well as operationalize tools and technologies that enable our team and&amp;nbsp;application to scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role, you will be managing services in a FedRAMP compliant environment, which &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;requires you to be a U.S. citizen. Additionally, this position may include work specified by the U.S. government that is restricted to U.S. citizens and must be conducted on U.S. territory.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership of the Bitwarden Gov cloud infrastructure, with emphasis on security, reliability and quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate current infrastructure and, on a regular basis, make recommendations for reliability, security, availability, scalability and cost management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement site reliability tools, monitoring, early warning and alert systems, and observability across Bitwarden Gov cloud environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to infrastructure based outages; participate and contribute to ongoing strategy for 24x7 support (This role has an on-call rotation with weekend shifts)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architectural designs and engineering operations at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active participation in code reviews, learning and spreading technical knowledge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute and mature incident management/escalation processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross functional teams to refine priorities and deliverables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and identify opportunities for new initiatives to support organizational needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create/maintain standard operational procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ongoing vulnerability management and security remediations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU BRING TO BITWARDEN&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 5 years of experience with FedRAMP (Moderate/High levels) - continuous monitoring, vulnerability management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sense of curiosity, resourcefulness, pragmatism&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Production experience with incident response, on-call rotations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge and understanding of cloud networking, traffic management (CNI, Istio)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise with multi-region deployments in public cloud environments (AWS/Azure/GCP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable production Kubernetes experience (Managed Kubernetes, Helm, kubectl, kOps, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI fluency with AI assisted workstreams and AI tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competency with least one programming language, such as C#, Python, Go, etc&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cloud deployment and automation tools/methodologies (i.e. GitOps, Terraform, Pulumi)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to maintain discretion, handle sensitive information, and improve security best-practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technocrat at heart, staying current with trends and new technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative and adaptable mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Openness and authenticity combined with excellent communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excitement and enthusiasm for open source and for better internet security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent problem-solving skills – you might not know all the answers, but you know how to find and communicate the possible solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NICE-TO-HAVES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with distributed monitoring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Startup experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open source experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;User of Bitwarden&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior SaaS experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT TO EXPECT IN THE INTERVIEW PROCESS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meeting with our Recruiting team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interview with SRE Manager&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interview(s) with SRE team panel&lt;/li&gt;
