&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A FEW REASONS TO WORK WITH US&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our user community loves us and we love them. Come to work each day with a sense of purpose as we bring a more secure internet experience to everyone from our friends and family to the world’s largest organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Become an expert. You’ll get immersed in the prominent technology markets of security and open source software. We are dedicated to building an incredible team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work remotely with motivated andinnovative team members and take part in productive and fun meetups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn and grow. Take on new challenges with the support of your team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In the United States, the starting base compensation range for this role is $140,000 - $185,000. Actual compensation may vary based on level, relevant experience, and skill set as assessed in the interview process, as well as market data by location. See our careers page for a list of benefits. Please note that compensation outside the U.S. will differ based on the market.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Bitwarden promotes better internet security and safety with the leading open source password management solution for individuals, teams, and business organizations. Our philosophy on security is that “we are all in this together” – we continue to offer a full-featured free version of Bitwarden so that everyone can be protected with strong password management. We also provide enterprise-grade solutions to some of the largest companies in the world, and will continue to innovate in the identity and authentication market as the world starts to grow beyond passwords. Read more on &lt;a href=&quot;https://bitwarden.com/blog/&quot;&gt;the Bitwarden blog&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Software Development Engineer in Test (SDET) on Bitwarden’s Autofill Coverage team,&amp;nbsp;you will help make autofill work reliably on the sites people actually use, and keep it fast and&amp;nbsp;unobtrusive as the product evolves. Autofill is the Bitwarden capability that fills logins,&amp;nbsp;payment details, and identities into web forms across browsers. The Autofill Coverage team&amp;nbsp;maintains and expands a curated dataset of site-specific autofill rules, builds automation that&amp;nbsp;continuously checks autofill across popular websites, and builds lab-based measurement of&amp;nbsp;autofill’s performance in the browser. Every engineer on the team works across all of this, so&amp;nbsp;we value curiosity and range over a perfect match to any single tool. This is a hands-on role.&amp;nbsp;You will spend your time writing, reviewing, and shipping code, alongside your teammatesand in close partnership with the wider Autofill team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU WILL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;UI Automation: Build and maintain browser automation that checks autofill across popular&amp;nbsp;real-world websites and purpose-built test pages. Keep suites stable as sites change, with&amp;nbsp;reliable locators, sensible waits, and flakiness fixed at its root.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance Testing: Run, extend, and maintain lab-based benchmarks that measure how&amp;nbsp;autofill affects page responsiveness, rendering, and memory in the browser. Set up runs,&amp;nbsp;review results, and investigate numbers that look wrong.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Trustworthy Results: Make sure test and benchmark results can be relied on. Confirm that&amp;nbsp;two runs did the same work before comparing them, and flag misleading metrics before&amp;nbsp;anyone acts on them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Test Scenarios: Build and maintain test pages that recreate tricky real-world patterns, such&amp;nbsp;as dynamic forms, shadow DOM, and iframes, so they can be tested repeatably.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Failure Triage: Reproduce autofill failures found by automation, support, or internal reports.&amp;nbsp;Document them clearly, hand dataset fixes to teammates, and route the rest to the right&amp;nbsp;owner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reporting and Observability: Publish results to dashboards, set up alerting on&amp;nbsp;regressions, and report coverage and trends on a regular cadence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-Assisted Development: Use AI coding assistants effectively in daily engineering and&amp;nbsp;exercise judgement about where they help and where they do not. Help keep test&amp;nbsp;documentation and Claude skills current as new autofill code lands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning and Collaboration: Pair with senior engineers on hard problems, share what you&amp;nbsp;learn, and review teammates’ pull requests with care.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-Functional Partnership: Work closely with Software Engineer teammates, the&amp;nbsp;Autofill team, Product, and Security on triage, test strategy, and release coordination.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU BRING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Overall Experience: 4–8 years in test automation, SDET, or software engineering roles, with hands-on UI automation of web applications and exposure to front-end performance&lt;br&gt;testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Stack: We value strong automation fundamentals and a performance mindset&amp;nbsp;over an exact tool match. Experience with load-testing tools such as JMeter or k6 is&amp;nbsp;welcome, but this role centres on performance inside the browser.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise-&amp;nbsp;UI automation with Playwright, Cypress, Selenium/WebDriver, or Puppeteer, including stable&amp;nbsp;locators, waits, and handling flaky tests&amp;nbsp;JavaScript or TypeScript, and Node.js&amp;nbsp;HTML, the DOM, and CSS selectors&lt;br&gt;Front-end performance testing with the Chrome DevTools Performance panel, Lighthouse,&amp;nbsp;WebPageTest, or Core Web Vitals tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience-&amp;nbsp;CI/CD with GitHub Actions, Jenkins, or similar, and running tests in Docker.&amp;nbsp;Interpreting performance results: percentiles, variance, and comparing runs fairly&amp;nbsp;Dashboards and alerting with Datadog, Grafana, New Relic, or similar.&amp;nbsp;Data or API validation with JSON Schema, Postman, or similar&amp;nbsp;AI-assisted development, preferably Claude Code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity-&amp;nbsp;Chrome DevTools Protocol and browser Performance APIs (PerformanceObserver, Long&amp;nbsp;Tasks, User Timing)&amp;nbsp;Browser extensions and how they are tested (Manifest V3)&amp;nbsp;Shell scripting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engineering Mindset: Curious about why a test failed, not just that it failed. You treat a flaky&amp;nbsp;test or a surprising number as something to understand rather than rerun until green, and&amp;nbsp;you pick up new tools quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience with containerized environments,&amp;nbsp;automated test frameworks (unit, integration, and end-to-end), CI/CD pipelines, and&amp;nbsp;observability tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Secure Coding: Familiarity with secure coding practices and care in handling test&amp;nbsp;credentials and sensitive data, with an interest in how security shapes product decisions in a&amp;nbsp;zero-knowledge product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative Spirit: A highly collaborative and adaptable mindset, excited to work in rapid,&amp;nbsp;outcome-driven feedback loops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open Source Passion: Excitement and enthusiasm for open source, developer advocacy,&amp;nbsp;and building a more secure internet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Problem-Solving: Excellent problem-solving skills, valuing written, clear documentation and&amp;nbsp;using data to make technical decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an opportunity to play a foundational role in shaping our India Engineering COE from the ground up. Our user community loves us and we love them. Come to work each day with a sense of purpose as we bring a more secure internet experience to everyone from our friends and family to the world’s largest organizations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Become an expert. You’ll get immersed in the prominent technology markets of security and open source software. You&#39;ll work alongside talented global teams, solve meaningful engineering challenges, influence how we scale our engineering organization &amp;amp; contribute to products used by customers around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;re passionate about building exceptional teams, enabling engineering excellence, and making a lasting impact within a fast-growing engineering company, we&#39;d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Employer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are committed to fostering an inclusive workplace where everyone can do their best work. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds and make employment decisions based on skills, experience, qualifications, and business needs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Bitwarden is the trusted identity security leader for millions of users worldwide, empowering enterprises, developers, and individuals to securely manage and share sensitive information anywhere. Bitwarden makes it easy for all users to extend robust security across their devices with password management, secrets management, and passwordless and passkey innovations. The company is headquartered in Santa Barbara, California with team members located across the globe. Learn more at &lt;a href=&quot;https://bitwarden.com/&quot;&gt;bitwarden.com&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior II Software Engineer on our Auth team, you will be responsible for developing and maintaining the core authentication systems for the Bitwarden clients - web, desktop, browser extension, CLI, and mobile apps. The Auth team owns code in our Angular clients, our shared Rust core, and our IdentityServer and API back-end, supporting password, SSO, passkey, and other authentication methods, as well as our 2FA and account management.&amp;nbsp; A candidate for this position should have very strong skills in Rust and Angular, working in complex and multi-client applications, as well as excellent communication and technical writing abilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a team of curious, passionate engineers who strive to solve difficult problems and enable success in others. If this sounds like you, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is an all-remote team and we’re looking for someone located in the U.S. We do not offer visa sponsorship at this time.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain our authentication code in our shared Rust core library, Angular clients, and IdentityServer back-end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scope and refine upcoming initiatives, working collaboratively across teams to design, document, and communicate forward-looking solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute constructively in team discussions - synchronous and asynchronous - building shared understanding and driving toward actionable results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide timely, thorough, and well-reasoned code reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Triage, diagnose, and resolve bugs reported by our community and our customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Update and validate core dependencies to ensure a secure and stable supply chain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU BRING TO BITWARDEN&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience developing in Angular/.NET experience a strong plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with integrating Rust into other clients using WASM and UNIFFI bindings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of modern web authentication concepts (OAuth 2.0, OIDC, WebAuthn)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with Claude/LLMs or an openness to learn how to work the technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical writing skills and the ability to clearly communicate complex problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attention to detail; we take our responsibility for authenticating our users very seriously&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of modern encryption techniques and principles of secure development are a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative and adaptable mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Openness and authenticity combined with excellent communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excitement and enthusiasm for open source and for better internet security&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent problem-solving skills – you might not know all the answers, but you know how to find and communicate the solution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT TO EXPECT IN THE INTERVIEW PROCESS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meeting with our Recruiting Manager&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interview with Auth team Engineering Manager and Platform Group Manager&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Panel interview with Auth team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A FEW REASONS TO WORK WITH US&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our user community loves us and we love them. Come to work each day with a sense of purpose as we bring a more secure internet experience to everyone from our friends and family to the world’s largest organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Become an expert. You’ll get immersed in the prominent technology markets of security and open source software.&lt;/li&gt;
