&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;In the United States, the starting base compensation range for this role is $140,000 - $200,000. Actual compensation may vary based on level, relevant experience, and skill set as assessed in the interview process, as well as market data by location. See our careers page for a list of benefits. Please note that compensation outside the U.S. will differ based on the market.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Bitwarden promotes better internet security and safety with the leading open source password management solution for individuals, teams, and business organizations. Our philosophy on security is that “we are all in this together” – we continue to offer a full-featured free version of Bitwarden so that everyone can be protected with strong password management. We also provide enterprise-grade solutions to some of the largest companies in the world, and will continue to innovate in the identity and authentication market as the world starts to grow beyond passwords. Read more on &lt;a href=&quot;https://bitwarden.com/blog/&quot;&gt;the Bitwarden blog&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Software Engineer on the Autofills side of this team, yyou will help make autofill work reliably on the sites people actually use, and keep it fast and unobtrusive as the&amp;nbsp;product evolves. Autofill is the Bitwarden capability that fills logins, payment details, and&amp;nbsp;identities into web forms across browsers. The Autofill Coverage team maintains and&amp;nbsp;expands a curated dataset of site-specific autofill rules, builds automation that continuously&lt;br&gt;checks autofill across popular websites, and builds lab-based measurement of autofill’s&amp;nbsp;performance in the browser. Every engineer on the team works across all of this, so we&amp;nbsp;value curiosity and range over a perfect match to any single tool. This is a hands-on role.You will spend your time writing, reviewing, and shipping code, alongside your teammates&amp;nbsp;and in close partnership with the wider Autofill team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU WILL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;End-to-End Delivery &amp;amp; Ownership: Own substantial pieces of the team’s work from&amp;nbsp;design through production: the site-specific rule dataset and its tooling, theautomation that continuously checks autofill on real websites and turns failures into&amp;nbsp;fixes, and the benchmarking harness that measures autofill’s performance impact&amp;nbsp;and responsiveness. Stay with your work once it is live.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automation at Scale: Design browser automation that runs reliably against real,&amp;nbsp;constantly changing websites. Handle flakiness, dynamic content, and anti-bot&amp;nbsp;measures, and turn results into actionable signal rather than noise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance Measurement: Build and improve lab-based benchmarks that&amp;nbsp;measure how autofill affects page responsiveness, rendering, and memory. Treat&amp;nbsp;measurement as engineering: control noise, question surprising numbers, and make&amp;nbsp;sure a metric means what it claims before anyone acts on it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engineering Standards and Automated Quality: Build and maintain the validation,&amp;nbsp;versioning, and CI checks that catch bad data and misleading results before they&amp;nbsp;ship. Review teammates’ pull requests with care and invite the same scrutiny of your&amp;nbsp;own. Keep documentation and contribution guidance in our open source repositories&amp;nbsp;clear.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Decoupled Architecture and Service Boundaries: Design the dataset so it can&amp;nbsp;evolve independently of client release cycles, with backward compatibility across&amp;nbsp;supported client versions. Keep test and measurement tooling cleanly separated&amp;nbsp;from the product code it exercises.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Mentorship: Pair on hard problems, share what you learn, and help&amp;nbsp;SDETs and newer engineers find their footing in a security-sensitive codebase.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-Assisted Development: Use AI coding assistants effectively in daily engineering&amp;nbsp;and exercise judgement about where they help and where they do not. Build assistive tooling that speeds up rule authoring, with a human always reviewing and&amp;nbsp;approving the result.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operational Stewardship: Triage autofill defects from support, internal reports,&amp;nbsp;automated checks, and benchmarks. Fix what belongs to the team and route the rest&amp;nbsp;to the right owner with clear attribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-Functional Partnership &amp;amp;amp; Collaboration: Partner closely with the Autofill&amp;nbsp;team, Product, Security, and SDET teammates to design and validate solutions&amp;nbsp;before implementation begins.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU BRING&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Overall Experience: 5–9 years building and operating production software, with a&amp;nbsp;track record of owning substantial, technically demanding work end to end as an&amp;nbsp;individual contributor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Stack: We hire for strength and mindset, not an exact tool match. You&amp;nbsp;should be strong in at least one of browser automation or front-end performance, and&amp;nbsp;keen to grow into the other.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise&lt;br&gt;– TypeScript or JavaScript, and Node.js&lt;br&gt;– The DOM, HTML forms, and CSS selectors, including how real-world pages&amp;nbsp;diverge from spec&lt;br&gt;– Browser automation with Playwright, Puppeteer, Selenium, or Cypress, or front-end performance analysis with Chrome DevTools, Lighthouse, and Core Web&amp;nbsp;Vitals&lt;br&gt;– CI/CD with GitHub Actions or a similar platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience&lt;br&gt;– Shell scripting and Docker&lt;br&gt;– Data validation with JSON Schema or similar, and maintaining versioned&amp;nbsp;datasets or configuration&lt;br&gt;– Reading performance data: percentiles, run-to-run variation, and telling a real&amp;nbsp;regression from noise&lt;br&gt;– Dashboards and alerting with Datadog, Grafana/Prometheus, New Relic, or&amp;nbsp;similar&lt;br&gt;– AI-assisted development, preferably Claude Code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity&lt;br&gt;– Browser internals such as rendering, garbage collection, the Chrome DevTools&amp;nbsp;Protocol, and Performance APIs (PerformanceObserver, Long Tasks, User&amp;nbsp;Timing)&lt;br&gt;– Browser extension architecture (Manifest V3, content scripts, extension&amp;nbsp;messaging)&lt;br&gt;– Front-end frameworks and tooling such as Lit, React, RxJS, and webpack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;T-Shaped Engineering Mindset: Depth in one area and genuine range across&amp;nbsp;others. You ask why, not just what; you treat a flaky test or a surprising number as&amp;nbsp;something to understand rather than hide; and you pick up new tools quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience with containerized environments, automated test frameworks&amp;nbsp;(unit, integration, and end-to-end), CI/CD pipelines, and observability tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Secure Coding: Familiarity with zero-trust and zero-knowledge security&amp;nbsp;architectures, encryption standards, and threat-modeling methodologies, and an understanding of why vetted, human-authored rules and heuristic-based autofill carry different security postures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative Spirit: A highly collaborative and adaptable mindset, excited to work&amp;nbsp;in rapid, outcome-driven feedback loops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open Source Passion: Excitement and enthusiasm for open source, developer&amp;nbsp;advocacy, and building a more secure internet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Problem-Solving: Excellent problem-solving skills, valuing written, clear&amp;nbsp;documentation and using data to make technical decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an opportunity to play a foundational role in shaping our India Engineering COE from the ground up. Our user community loves us and we love them. Come to work each day with a sense of purpose as we bring a more secure internet experience to everyone from our friends and family to the world’s largest organizations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Become an expert. You’ll get immersed in the prominent technology markets of security and open source software. You&#39;ll work alongside talented global teams, solve meaningful engineering challenges, influence how we scale our engineering organization &amp;amp; contribute to products used by customers around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;re passionate about building exceptional teams, enabling engineering excellence, and making a lasting impact within a fast-growing engineering company, we&#39;d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Employer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are committed to fostering an inclusive workplace where everyone can do their best work. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds and make employment decisions based on skills, experience, qualifications, and business needs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Bitwarden is the trusted identity security leader for millions of users worldwide, empowering enterprises, developers, and individuals to securely manage and share sensitive information anywhere. Bitwarden makes it easy for all users to extend robust security across their devices with password management, secrets management, and passwordless and passkey innovations. The company is headquartered in Santa Barbara, California with team members located across the globe. Learn more at &lt;a href=&quot;https://bitwarden.com/&quot;&gt;bitwarden.com&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Full Stack Engineer on the Data Insights and Reporting (DIRT) team at Bitwarden, your work will directly impact how enterprise administrators understand the security posture of their organizations. You&#39;ll build the reports, dashboards, and integrations that turn vault data and activity into actionable intelligence, surfacing at-risk credentials, mapping who has access to what, protecting users from phishing attacks directly in the browser, and streaming events into the SIEM and collaboration tools security teams already rely on. This role combines deep front-end craft, backend API and data work, and the challenge of building meaningful insights on top of a zero-knowledge, end-to-end encrypted product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working within Bitwarden&#39;s open-source ecosystem, you&#39;ll collaborate with a passionate community dedicated to transparency and trust in security software while contributing to our mission of making security accessible to everyone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an all-remote team and we&#39;re looking for someone located in the U.S. We do not offer visa sponsorship at this time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work collaboratively to build and maintain features across Access Intelligence, event integrations, the browser extension&#39;s phishing blocker, our shared Rust core library, and the Bitwarden Splunk app&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership of your work, partnering with QA to ensure that the appropriate parts of the application are tested and that tests are complete&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and evolve APIs, data models, and encrypted report structures that hold up to real enterprise-scale data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review PRs and provide constructive, pointed feedback to help fellow team members grow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the Bitwarden open-source community to review community contributions and address issues in GitHub&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU BRING TO BITWARDEN&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience with .NET Core and C# for backend services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency with Angular, TypeScript, and RxJS for front-end development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of relational database design, optimization, and SQL Server&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to design and implement RESTful APIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building features for enterprise customers where auditability, permissions, and compliance matter&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative and adaptable mindset with excellent communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excitement and enthusiasm for open source and for better internet security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent problem-solving skills – you might not know all the answers, but you know how to find and communicate the solution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NICE-TO-HAVES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;User of Bitwarden&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Startup experience&lt;/li&gt;
